arning to use your power, but where would you go to study? The Hero Academy, of course! But what would you do if you were one of the 20 percent who were born Quirkless?\nL26: 【17†Kohei Horikoshi】 was born in Aichi, Japan, in 1986. He received a Tezuka Award Honorable Mention in 2006, and after publishing several short stories in Akamaru Jump, his first serialized work in Weekly Shonen Jump was Oumagadoki Doubutsuen in 2010. Barrage was his second series and My Hero Academia his third series in Weekly Shonen Jump.\nL27: \nL28: 【18†Image†de7i3bh7bgh0d.cloudfront.net】\nL29: ### Plus Ultra! Artwork Spanning All 42 Volumes!\nL30: \nL31: Own the ultimate love letter to fans with My Hero Academia: Ultra Artworks.\nL32: \nL33: 【19†Watch trailer】\nL34: \nL35: 【20†Order now】\nL36: \nL37: 【21†Image†de7i3bh7bgh0d.cloudfront.net】\nL38: \nL39: ### All Might Tests his Teaching Mettle\nL40: \nL41: Plus more super stories in the final volume of My Hero Academia: Team-Up Missions.\nL42: \nL43: 【22†Read preview】\nL44: \nL45: 【23†Order now】\nL46: \nL47: 【24†Image†de7i3bh7bgh0d.cloudfront.net】\nL48: ### The End of an Era\nL49: \nL50: Uncover their endings, the reconstruction, and more in My Hero Academia, Vol. 42!\nL51: \nL52: 【19†Watch trailer】\nL53: \nL54: 【25†Read preview】\nL55: \nL56: 【26†Image†de7i3bh7bgh0d.cloudfront.net】\nL57: \nL58: ### The Collector’s Guide to My Hero Academia, Vol. 42\nL59: \nL60: Find exclusive covers and goodies for the final volume!\nL61: \nL62: 【27†Learn more】\nL63: \nL64: 【28†Image†de7i3bh7bgh0d.cloudfront.net】\nL65: \nL66: ### Make Your Art Plus Ultra!!\nL67: \nL68: With My Hero Academia: The Official Easy Illustration Guide.\nL69: \nL70: 【19†Watch trailer】\nL71: \nL72: 【29†Order now】\nL73: ### Read My Hero Academia\nL74: #### My Hero Academia: Ultra Artworks\nL75: Spanning ten years of Kohei Horikoshi’s work on his incredibly popular love letter to superheroes, My Hero Academia: Ultra Artworks includes covers, illustrations from Shonen Jump, and art fro